        "question_text": "Q.64 \n \n \n \n \nConsider a function \ud835\udc53: (0,1) \u2192{0, 1} defined as follows.  \nFor a real number  \ud835\udc5f\u2208(0,1) , \ud835\udc53(\ud835\udc5f) = 1 if the second digit after the decimal point \nin \ud835\udc5f is one of the four digits 2, 3, 6 and 7. Otherwise, \ud835\udc53(\ud835\udc5f) is equal to 0. \nThe number of points in (0,1) at which \ud835\udc53 is discontinuous is ___________. (answer \nin integer)",
